# Line-ending normalisation.

# Why this matters for this repository: the Kubernetes charts, the workflow files and the shell
# scripts are all consumed on Linux — by Helm, by GitHub Actions runners, and by the build
# server. A shell script checked out with CRLF endings fails on Linux with
# "/bin/bash^M: bad interpreter", which is a confusing error for what is really a line-ending
# problem. Declaring the expected endings here means the repository is correct regardless of
# which machine checked it out.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts genuinely want CRLF.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary files must not be normalised at all.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.jar binary
*.gz binary
*.zip binary
*.tgz binary